In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x) = \sech{x}$ and $v(x) = 4x.$ 

Therefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:

$$
 egin{aligned} egin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & = rac{{u}^{′}(x)\cdot v(x)-u(x)\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \  & = rac{{(	ext{\sech}x)}^{′}\cdot (4x)-	ext{\sech}x\cdot {(4x)}^{′}}{{(4x)}^{2}} \  & = rac{(-	ext{\sech}x\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)\cdot (4x)-	ext{\sech}x\cdot 4}{16{x}^{2}} \  & =- rac{4	ext{\sech}x(x\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+1)}{16{x}^{2}} \  & =- rac{	ext{\sech}x(x\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+1)}{4{x}^{2}}\end{aligned}\end{aligned}
$$
